king philippe is the first belgian  monarch to express regret for his  country's past in the democratic  republic of congo  but his speech to the congolese  parliament in the capital kinshasa  stopped short of apologizing for the  violence and exploitation of belgium's  75-year colonial rule  it led to violent acts and humiliations  on the occasion of my first trip to  congo right here in front of the  congolese people and those who still  suffer today i wish to reaffirm my  deepest regrets for those wounds of the  past  king philippe and his wife queen matild  are on a six-day visit the monarch and  congolese president felix chisiketti  have spoken about cooperation and  development  they haven't mentioned the role of king  philippe's great-grandfather's brother  belgian king leopold ii  he turned congo into his personal  fiefdom in 1885  he made a fortune from rubber  which congolese were forced to harvest  from the forests their hands were cut  off if they didn't collect enough for  their rulers  up to 10 million people died it was the  black lives matter movement two years  ago that prompted activists to deface  statues of king leopold in belgium  some of the statues were removed and  king philippe expressed regret for the  first time  [Applause]  two years later he's visiting democratic  republic of congo for the first time  he brought back a mask one of thousands  of artifacts looted by the colonialists  he said it's on a permanent loan from a  belgian museum  for some congolese it falls far short of  making up for the past so the atrocity  of the red rubber the whipping the  repetitive humiliation suffered by our  ancestor our funding fathers and mothers  should not  become a case that goes unnoticed  because they refuse to formally  apologize  for president chisiketi it brings some  international credibility he took office  two and a half years ago after elections  that leaked documents appeared to show  were rigged belgium's prime minister  who's also on the visit was critical at  the time  relations have since improved  i believe that for the democratic  republic of congo and i have always said  this the gateway to europe i am talking  about diplomatic and political europe  business europe is belgium  belgium's rule in congo was one of the  bloodiest chapters of european  colonialism and one of its most  profitable with vast amounts of wealth  looted  but belgium has been among the slowest  of european powers to even start to  acknowledge the past  malcolm webb al jazeera
 

